    "chunk_text": "Clause 5 : This clause amends section 72 of the principal enactment, and is consequentialto the amendment made by inserting section 19C in the principal enactment.\n\nClause 6 : This clause amends section 75 of the principal enactment, and is consequentialto the amendment made by inserting section 19C in the principal enactment.\n\n1Trusts (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n2\u2014PL 010391\u2014475 (10/2017)\n\nShort title.\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 24/2016\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE TRUSTS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 87)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Trusts (Amendment)Act, No. of 2017.\n\n2.Section 3 of the Trusts Ordinance (Chapter 87)(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is herebyamended by the repeal of paragraph (e) of that section andthe substitution therefor of the following paragraphs:-\n\n\u201c(e)\u201cbeneficiary\u201d means a person, or a defined ordefinitely ascertainable class of persons, for whosebenefit the confidence is accepted;\n\n(ee)\u201cprescribed\u201d means prescribed by regulations madeunder this Act;\u201d .\n\n3.The following new sections are hereby insertedimmediately after section 6 of the principal enactment andshall have effect as sections 6A and 6B of that enactment:-\n\n6A. (1) The Registrar-General shall prepareand maintain a register containing suchinformation as may be prescribed of every trust,created in compliance with section 5.\n\n(2) The trustee of any immovable ormovable property shall forward to the Registrar-General for the purpose of subsection (1), allsuch information relating to the trust, as maybe prescribed.\n\nAmendmentof section 3of Chapter87.\n\nInsertion ofnew sections6A and 6B inthe principalenactment.\n\n\u201cRegistrar-General tomaintain aregister oftrusts.\n\nTrusts (Amendment)2\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nDuty of theRegistrar-General toprovideinformationof trusts."
