    "chunk_text": "(d)any other information, the revealingof which would not adversely affectthe conduct of further investigationsand the interests of justice.\n\n(5) Any such Attorney-at-Law shall beentitled to\u2013\n\n(a)make representations on behalf ofsuch person being held in policecustody, to the officer in charge ofthe police station;\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n3Code of Criminal Procedure (Special Provisions)(Amendment)\n\n(c)have access to the person being heldin police custody, as provided for insubsections (6), (7), (8), (9) and (10).\n\n(6) Any such Attorney-at-Law shall, if he sorequests, be allowed to have access to theperson being held in police custody. However,such access may be delayed, if the officer incharge of the police station has reasonablegrounds to believe that the exercise of suchright of access at the time such right is soughtto be exercised\u2013\n\n(a)may lead to destruction of,interference with, or harm to theevidence that is connected with thecommitting of a cognizable offence,or may interfere with or cause anythreat or harm to any person whomay be acquainted with the facts andcircumstances pertaining to thecommission of such offence; or\n\n(b)may lead to the alerting of otherpersons who may have committedor, being concerned in thecommission of such cognizableoffence or other offences committedin the course of the same transaction,and who have not been arrested inthat regard; or\n\n(c)may hinder the identification,location or recovery of any propertyobtained by the commission ofcognizable offence, or the valuethereof or part thereof; or\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nCode of Criminal Procedure (Special Provisions)(Amendment)4\n\n(d)may hinder the identification,location or recovery of any weaponor other utensil used in thecommission of such cognizableoffence.\n\n(7) In any event, an Attorney-at-Law shallbe allowed access to the person in policecustody before the expiry of the time period,within which such person is to be producedbefore a Magistrate as provided for, by law."
