    "chunk_size_bytes": 1884,
    "chunk_text": "Clause 18 : This clause amends section 26 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to widen the regulation making power for theimplementation of standards stipulated in International conventions and agreements.\n\nClause 20 : This clause amends section 27 of the principal enactment by the insertionof new section 27A and the legal effect of that section as amended is to establish a fundcalled and known as Fisheries Reward Fund.\n\nClause 21 : This clause amends section 28 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to include new definitions to the expressions \u201cabandonedforeign fishing boat\u201d and \u201cDirector General\u201d and to substitute definitions for the expressions\u201cfish\u201d, \u201cfishing\u201d, \u201clocal fishing boat\u201d, \u201crelated activities\u201d, \u201cSecretary\u201d and \u201cSri LankaWaters\u201d.\n\n1Fisheries (Regulation of Foreign Fishing Boats)\n\n(Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n2\u2014PL 010405\u2014475 (10/2017)\n\nShort title.\n\n20\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 20/2016\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE FISHERIES (REGULATION OF FOREIGN FISHINGBOATS) ACT, NO. 59 OF 1979\n\nBe it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Fisheries (Regulation ofForeign Fishing Boats) (Amendment) Act, No. of 2017.\n\n2.The Fisheries (Regulation of Foreign FishingBoats)Act, No. 59 of 1979 (hereinafter referred to as the\u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is hereby amended by thesubstitution for the word \u201cSecretary\u201d wherever that wordoccurs in the principal enactment or any regulation, rule,notice or notifications of the word \u201cDirector-General\u201d.\n\n3.Section 3 of the principal enactment is herebyamended as follows:-\n\n(i)by the repeal of marginal note to that section andthe substitution therefor of the following:-\n\n\u201cArmed forces etc. to co-operate in implementationand enforcement of this Act.\u201d;"
