    "chunk_text": "(i) to conduct lectures, seminars, discussions exhibitionsand carnivals to promote the objects of thecorporation.\n\n(j) to liaise and co-ordinate with other local and foreigninstitutions which have similar objectives.\n\nNimal Rupasinghe Friendship Foundation(Incorporation)3\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n5.(1) The affairs of the corporation shall, subject to theother provisions of this Act and the rules in force for the timebeing of the corporation be administered by a Board ofDirectors Consisting of Chairman and Secretary, Treasurerand another eleven members elected in accordance with suchrules.\n\n(2) The Executive committee which held the office of thecorporation before the date of implementation of the Act,shall be the first Executive committeee of the corporation.\n\n6.(1) It shall be lawful for the Corporation, from time totime, at any General Meeting of the Corporation and by amajority of not less than two-thirds of the members presentand voting, to make rules, not inconsistent with theprovisions of this Act or any other written law, for all or anyof the following matters :\u2014\n\n(a)classification of membership, admission,withdrawal, expulsion or resignation of membersand membership fees payable ;\n\nManagementof the affairsof theCorporation.\n\nGeneralpowers of theCorporation.\n\nRules of theCorporation.\n\n4Nimal Rupasinghe Friendship Foundation(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(b)procedure to be observed for the summoning andholding of meetings of the Corporation and of theExecutive committee the quorum of such meetingsand the exercise and performance of their powersand duties ;\n\n(c)the appointment, power, duties and functions ofthe various officers, agents and servants of theCorporation ;\n\n(d)qualification required to become a member of theCorporation and the executive committee; and\n\n(e)the administration and management of the propertyof the Corporation."
