    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Justice on 03rd of April, 2018.\n\n(Published in the Gazette on March 14, 2018)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed.\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\n2-2d\n\n2-\n\nPRESCRIPTION (SPECIAL PROVISIONS)(AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Prescription (Special Provisions) Act, No. 5 of 2016.\n\nPrice : Rs. 6.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\n[Bill No. 238]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2: This clause amends section 4 of the Prescription (Special Provisions)Act, No. 5 of 2016 in order to extend the time period within which a disadvantaged personis entitled to avail himself of the benefits of the Act.\n\n1Prescription (Special Provisions)(Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n2\u2014PL 010708\u2014475 (03/2018)\n\nShort title.\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 39/2017\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE PRESCRIPTION (SPECIAL PROVISIONS)ACT, NO. 5 OF 2016\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Prescription (SpecialProvisions) (Amendment) Act, No. of 2018.\n\n2.Section 4 of the Prescription (Special Provisions) Act,No. 5 of 2016 is hereby amended as follows:\u2014\n\n(1)by the substitution for the words \u201ctwo years afterthe coming into operation of this Act.\u201d of the words\u201cfour years from the date of coming into operationof this Act.\u201d;\n\n(2)by the substitution for the words \u201ctwo years afterthe date of operation of this Act.\u201d, in the marginalnote to that section, of the words \u201cfour years fromthe date of coming into operation of this Act.\u201d.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nAmendmentof section 4of Act, No. 5of 2016.\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency.\n\nPrescription (Special Provisions)(Amendment)2\n\nDEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING"
