    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of July 26, 2018\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 26.07.2018)\n\nINSTITUTE OF PERSONNEL MANAGEMENT,SRI LANKA (AMENDMENT)\n\nOrdered to be published by the Minister of Labour, Trade Union Relationsand Sabaragamuwa Development\n\nto amend the Institute of Personnel Management, Sri LankaLaw, No. 24 of 1976\n\nPrice : Rs. 12.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nThis Gazette Supplement can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nA\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends the Institute of Personnel Management, Sri Lanka,Law, No. 24 of 1976 in order to change the name of that institute.\n\nClause 3 : This is consequential to the amendment made to the above Act, by clause 2.\n\nInstitute of Personnel Management,Sri Lanka (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 7/2018\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE INSTITUTE OF PERSONNEL MANAGEMENT,SRI LANKA LAW, NO. 24 OF 1976\n\nWHEREAS the members of the Institute of PersonnelManagement, Sri Lanka, incorporated by the institute ofPersonnel Management, Sri Lanka Law, No. 24 of 1976 havepassed a resolution to amend its name :\n\nAND WHEREAS the Institute of Personnel Management,Sri Lanka has applied to amend its name in order to giveeffect to such resolution, it will be expedient to grant suchapplication:\n\nNOW THEREFORE be it enacted by the Parliament of theDemocratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Institute of PersonnelManagement, Sri Lanka (Amendment) Act, No. of 2018.\n\n2.(1) The Institute of Personnel Management, Sri LankaLaw, No. 24 of 1976 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipalenactment\u201d) is hereby amended by the substitution for thewords \u201cInstitute of Personnel Management, Sri Lanka\u201dwherever they appear in the principal enactment of the words\u201cChartered Institute of Personnel Management, Sri Lanka\u201d."
