    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Internal & Home Affairs andProvincial Councils & Local Government on 04th of September, 2019\n\n(Published in the Gazette on June 10, 2019)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPrice : Rs. 6.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n[Bill No. 296]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nIMMIGRANTS AND EMIGRANTS(AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Immigrants and Emigrants Act (Chapter 351)\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2: This clause amends section 14 of the Immigrants and Emigrants Act(Chapter 351) and the legal effect of that clause is to increase the period of a visa and tomake provisions for the Minister to determine the period of permanent residence visa.\n\nImmigrants and Emigrants(Amendment)1\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 24/2018\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE IMMIGRANTS AND EMIGRANTS ACT(CHAPTER 351)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Immigrants and Emigrants(Amendment) Act, No. of 2019.\n\n2.Section 14 of the Immigrants and Emigrants Act(Chapter 351) is hereby amended as follows:-\n\n(1)in subsection (1) thereof, by the substitution for thewords, \u201ctwo years,\u201d of the words \u201cfive years,\u201d;\n\n(2)in subsection (2) thereof, by the substitution for thewords, \u201cexceeding two years but not exceeding fiveyears,\u201d of the words \u201cexceeding five years but notexceeding ten years,\u201d; and\n\n(3)by the insertion immediately after subsection (3)thereof, of the following subsection:-\n\n\u201c(3A) (a) Notwithstanding the time limitsspecified in subsections (1) and (2), the periodof permanent residence visa may be determinedby the Minister.\n\n(b) For the purpose of paragraph (a),\u201cpermanent residence visa\u201d means a visa grantedunder regulations made under this Act.\u201d."
