    "chunk_text": "(l)is or becomes a director, officer or employee of afinancial institution operating through offices inSri Lanka, a beneficial owner of an equity interestin a financial institution or a beneficial owner offive percent or more of an equity interest in anyother financial institution.\n\n19.Any person serving any office referred to insubsection (1) of section 16 may resign such office by givingnot less than three months\u2019 notice in writing to the President.\n\n20.(1) Any person appointed under subsections (1) and(2) of section 16 shall cease to hold such office upon theoccurrence of anything referred to in subsection (2) ofsection 18.\n\nDisqualificationsand removalfrom office.\n\n30\n\n19Central Bank of Sri Lanka\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(2) Any person appointed under subsection (1) of section16 may be removed by the President, upon a writtenrecommendation of the Governing Board, in the event theGoverning Board is satisfied, following a hearing of therelevant appointed person that such person\u2013\n\n(a)is unable to exercise, discharge and perform thepowers, functions and duties of such office becauseof an infirmity of body or mind that has lasted formore than a period of three months;\n\n(b)has not complied with the relevant code of conductof the Central Bank;\n\n(c)has failed to exercise, discharge and perform thepowers, functions and duties of such office for aconsecutive period of more than three monthswithout approval of the Governing Board; or\n\n(d)is disqualified in terms of the provisions ofsubsection (2) of section 18.\n\n(3) Any person appointed under subsection (2) of section16 may be removed from office, with the concurrence of theMinister, upon a decision of the Governing Board, in theevent the Governing Board is satisfied following a hearingof the relevant person that such person\u2013\n\n(a)is unable to exercise, discharge and perform thepowers, functions and duties of such office becauseof an infirmity of body or mind that has lasted formore than a period of three months;"
