    "chunk_text": "128. (1) Notwithstanding the prohibition in section 87of this Act, the Central Bank may make new directprovisional advances to the Government to financeexpenditures authorized to be incurred out of theConsolidated Fund within the first month of the financialyear:\n\nContinuationof terms ofoffice.\n\nProvisionaladvances.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nCentral Bank of Sri Lanka95\n\nexceed ten per centum of the revenue of the first four monthsof the preceding financial year as reported in the half yearlyreport published by the Ministry of the Minister under theFiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No. 3 of 2003 forthe relevant period.\n\n(2) Such new advances shall bear interest at prevailingmarket-related rates as determined by the Central Bank.\n\n(3) Such new advances shall not be made to refinancethe outstanding credit of the Central Bank to the Governmenton the appointed date.\n\n(4) The provisions of subsections (1), (2) and (3) of thissection shall be effective until such time provisions are madeby law for the Government to finance its immediate fiscalrequirements.\n\n129. (1) Notwithstanding the prohibition in subsection(1) of section 87, any outstanding credit of the Central Bankto the Government as at the appointed date may bemaintained.\n\n(2) The Central Bank shall, in consultation with theMinister, convert any outstanding credit of the Central Bankto the Government as at the appointed date, over a period often years immediately succeeding such date, into negotiabledebt instruments with a specified maturity period issued atprevailing market-related interest rates, on which the CentralBank shall, as much as possible sell such debt instrumentsunder its monetary policy."
