    "chunk_text": "3.Section 4 of the Principal Law is hereby amended byrepealing it and by the substitution of the following:-\n\n\u201c4.the declaration of assets and liabilities shall betendered in the following manner:-\n\n(a)to the Speaker -\n\nii.Members of the Parliament;\n\n(b)to the President -\n\ni.the person referred to in paragraph (b),(c), (e), (f), (g) and (i) of Section 2 (1) ofthis Law;\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n4Declaration of Assets and Liabilities (Amendment)\n\n(c)to the Judicial Service Commission -\n\ni.officers referred to in paragraph (h) ofSection 2 (1) of this Law;\n\n(d)to the Secretary of the relevant Ministry -\n\ni.officers referred to in paragraph (j), (k),(n), (o), (p), (q), (r) and (s) of Section 2(1) of this Law;\n\n(e)to the Election Commission -\n\ni.the person referred to in (l) and (m) ofSection 2 (1) of this Law.\u201d.\n\n4.Section 9 (1) of the Principle Law is hereby amendedby deleting the words \u201cnot exceeding Thousand Rupees\u201dand by the substitution the words \u201cnot exceeding OneHundred Thousand Rupees\u201d.\n\n5.Section 10 (1) of the Principle Law is hereby amendedby deleting the words \u201cthe Minister may make regulation\u201dand by the substitution of the words \u201cthe President maymake regulations\u201d.\n\n6.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency.\n\nDeclaration of Assets and Liabilities (Amendment)5\n\nDepartment of Government Printing"
