    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 321]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by Hon. (Dr.) Mrs. Thusitha Wijemanne, M.P.for Kegalle District on 05th of February 2020\n\n(Published in the Gazette on January 13, 2020)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 12.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nLAND DEVELOPMENT (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Land Development Ordinance (Chapter 464)\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nLand Development (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nShort title.\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE LAND DEVELOPMENT ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 464)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows: -\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Land Development(Amendment) Act, No. of 2020.\n\n2.Rule 1(b) and rule 2 of the Third Schedule of theprincipal Act should be replaced with the following rules:-\n\n\u201c1(b). Title to a holding for the purposes of Section 72shall devolve on the relatives of the permit holder orowner in the order of priority in which they are respectivelymentioned in the subjoined table, the older beingpreferred to the younger if there are more relatives thanone in any group:\n\nProvided that nothing in this rule should give priorityto the older person when a land has been developed byother person than the older person.\n\nTable\n\n(i)Children;\n\n(ii)Grand sons and daughters;\n\n(iii)Parents;\n\n(iv) Brothers and Sisters;\n\n(v) Uncles and Aunts;\n\n(vi) Nephews and Nieces.\n\nIn this rule \u201crelative\u201d means, a relative by blood and notby marriage and \u201cchildren\u201d includes adopted children too.\n\nAmendmentof ThirdSchedule ofChapter 464.\n\n2Land Development (Amendment)\n\n5"
